# scenarios/10_small_company.books: loaded by ledger_server into 10_small_company.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	10. A small company's year, from the founders' money to the income tax
about	One year of a small trading company, each kind of transaction once: the founders' capital and a bank loan; equipment bought; goods bought on credit and sold with VAT; rent and salaries paid, with the social security and withholding tax passed on; the loan repaid with interest; the VAT return.
about	Then the year end: the goods still in stock are counted (609), the equipment is depreciated, and the income tax on the profit is owed. The profit of 31,600 less 6,320 of tax leaves 25,280 for the owners.
currency	USD
